==Acquisition==
*This mod can be acquired by attaining the rank of '''General''' under {{Faction|Steel Meridian}}, or the rank of '''Exalted''' under {{Faction|Red Veil}}, and spending {{sc|25,000}} to purchase.
*This mod can periodically be acquired from [[The Circuit]].

==Notes==
*Damage bonus is affected by [[Ability Strength]].
*Duration is affected by [[Ability Duration]].
*Range is affected by [[Ability Range]].
*Cannot be equipped at the same time as {{M|Revealing Spores}}.
*Adds {{D|Corrosive}} damage to the weapon, added alongside IPS and elemental mods.
**Does not increase the damage of most abilities, including [[Exalted Weapon|Exalted Weapons]].
**Does not merge with {{D|Toxin}} or {{D|Electricity}}.
**For example: for a weapon with a base damage of 100 {{D|Impact}} per bullet, with the mod {{M|Infected Clip}} at max rank, and the buff from Venom Dose at max rank with 110 strength, the damage will be: 100 {{D|Impact}}, 90 {{D|Toxin}}, and 110 {{D|Corrosive}}.
***In this situation, if a status procs, it will have 100/300 chance to be {{D|Impact}}, 90/300 chance to be {{D|Toxin}}, and 110/300 to be {{D|Corrosive}}.
*For more information on how this augment works, see [[Buff & Debuff#Elemental damage bonus|Buff &amp; Debuff]] page.
*Multiple casts of Venom Dose do not stack; the buff with the highest Ability Strength will take effect.
**However if a weaker one with more Ability Duration is cast, it will take effect after the stronger buff expires.

